    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "beaa1997_789e1a43",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/config.proto",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-24T22:14:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e When it\u0027s a broken address, why let it have that quirk?\n\nThe address will still be used normally by rootcanal, but inspecting the pcap trace you should be able to notice immediately if the default address leaked into baseband packets.\n\n\u003e bb:aa:dd:bb:aa:dd\n\nLooks good 😊",
      "parentUuid": "5fc62a9b_b2d58067",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "2320be8828f5a34573505c70396c7d2a7446e911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01afeb02_3971e3c8",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/config.proto",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-24T21:34:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does each connection to this port give you a controller of this type, or are we changing things so that you need a port per controller?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "2320be8828f5a34573505c70396c7d2a7446e911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe9d8281_de27cdde",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/config.proto",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-24T21:40:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Each connection gives a controller with the specified type.\nThe equivalent to the current setup __ and the default I will put int place __ would be `Controller { tcp_port: 6402, preset: DEFAULT }`.\n\nHaving multiple ports enables testing with heterogeneous configurations. e.g. mixing extended and legacy scanning capabilities, verifying proper validation of remote capabilities, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "01afeb02_3971e3c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "2320be8828f5a34573505c70396c7d2a7446e911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff8b1e42_6ff1653f",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/config.proto",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-24T21:43:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s one way to do it.  The reason I asked is because I could also imagine configuring and connecting until you had enough controllers.\n\nOne port:\n- Configure\n- Connect\n- Configure\n- Connect\n...\n\nI\u0027m wondering what the benefit of multiple ports is, compared to that.\n\nI\u0027m thinking about GRPC-based connections as well.",
      "parentUuid": "fe9d8281_de27cdde",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "2320be8828f5a34573505c70396c7d2a7446e911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "924ec247_1720f6b3",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/config.proto",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-24T21:48:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would like to avoid adding the requirement that a gRPC connection must be established to configure the controller. Netsim is already adding this feature, I think adding it to rootcanal would be redundant.\n\nI thought about adding a vendor command to set the preferred configuration at boot time, but that requires modifying the host.\n\nHaving multiple ports is the same as having multiple devices, and connecting to one.",
      "parentUuid": "ff8b1e42_6ff1653f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "2320be8828f5a34573505c70396c7d2a7446e911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
